From 1975b063ba47d6deff7411a59dddfbc5f1a802e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:44:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 233/291] Part: pointsInside and rayCast, fast batch queries on
 shapes

Part.pointsInside(shape, points, tolerance, method='auto') classifies many points at
once: a bounding box test, then the parity of a ray's crossings with a triangulation
in a bounding volume tree, and BRepClass3d_SolidClassifier only for points within
twice the deflection of the surface (method 'exact': the classifier for all, in
parallel; 'mesh': never).  100,000 points on a filleted part with a hole: 0.16 s
(Shape.isInside in a loop: about 52 s), same answers as isInside.

Part.rayCast(shapes, origin, direction, all=False) returns the nearest hit (or all)
with distance, shape index, face index, exact point and outward normal; origins and
directions may be lists.  The tree finds the face, IntCurvesFace_Intersector the
point.  100,000 rays: 0.16 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
